From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Le Hoang Quyen <lehoangquyen@chromium.org>
Date: Wed, 16 Sep 2026 08:45:41 -0700
Subject: Skip Graphite async read pixels callback when context is lost

Check delegate->IsContextLost() in ReadPixelsCallbackThreadSafe and
skip invoking the callback if the context has been lost. This avoids
a potential stack use-after-free in the callback when the caller of
asyncRescaleAndReadPixels* has already returned early due to context
loss.

Bug: 561997427
Change-Id: I3d58691fd035e6f68c708353d55494f3ea40eae0
Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8409528
Reviewed-by: Colin Blundell <blundell@chromium.org>
Reviewed-by: Kyle Charbonneau <kylechar@chromium.org>
Commit-Queue: Quyen Le <lehoangquyen@google.com>
Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1698970}

Electron adaptation notes (42-x-y):
- Applied on top of the picked prerequisite 'Graphite: Add Delegate interface
  and handle context loss in readback' (cherry-pick-c7e7ee40de40.patch).
- graphite_shared_context.cc: the branch has no
  asyncRescaleAndReadPixelsYUV420AndSubmit / ...YUVA420AndSubmit overloads,
  so the four one-line hunks touching those functions are dropped. Every
  CreateAsyncReadContextThreadSafe() call on the branch now passes delegate_;
  the callback/context-lost changes merged verbatim.

